Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.40,0:00:07.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandmother said an emperor camped under\NMount Tossa saw a comet, and named the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.56,0:00:09.49,Default,,0,0,0,,place Dessie: my joy.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.40,0:00:18.43,Default,,0,0,0,,At seven, I made a comet of my own:\Nold socks, plastic bags and string.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.40,0:00:26.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing in Dessie is flat. Even our\Nfootball pitch climbed the mountain.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.40,0:00:34.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Our rule: kick it in the ditch, you\Nclimb in after it. Hayat's left foot is
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.68,0:00:37.43,Default,,0,0,0,,the reason that rule exists.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.19,0:00:48.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Four–four. Next goal wins. Then the fog\Ncame down from Tossa like a white gabi.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.19,0:00:55.94,Default,,0,0,0,,I couldn't see anything but my comet. I\Nkicked it with all I had. It vanished
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.94,0:00:59.13,Default,,0,0,0,,into the fog. “GOAL!” shouted Dawit.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.90,0:01:07.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandmother laughed and pulled me under\Nher gabi: “A comet doesn't stay. It only
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.83,0:01:10.74,Default,,0,0,0,,shows you where your joy is.”
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.53,0:01:17.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Today, when people ask where I'm from, I\Nsay Dessie. And then I tell them what it
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.77,0:01:18.24,Default,,0,0,0,,means.
